freeglut — OSMesa (headless, off-screen) backend
=================================================

Normally freeglut creates the GL context through the platform's native window
system (GLX/X11, WGL/Windows, NSOpenGL/Cocoa, EGL/GLES). The OSMesa backend
instead uses OSMesa ("Off-Screen Mesa"), which renders into a plain CPU memory
buffer with NO X11/GLX/Cocoa/EGL and no display server. The result is a
software (llvmpipe/swrast) **compatibility** GL context, so fixed-function
rendering, freeglut's glutSolid*/glutWire* shapes, and glRenderMode(GL_FEEDBACK)
all work — which makes it ideal for headless CI (e.g. validating geometry or
feedback output with no display).

It is enabled with the CMake option FREEGLUT_OSMESA, is OS-agnostic (Linux,
macOS, Windows), and is mutually exclusive with the FREEGLUT_GLES,
FREEGLUT_WAYLAND and FREEGLUT_COCOA options (CMake errors out if they are
combined).

(If you only want freeglut's geometry/font drawing without any windowing — for
an environment that already emulates GLUT windowing, such as Emscripten — see
the separate standalone "glutshapes" library in README.glutshapes.)


Dependencies
------------

Just OSMesa — the headless build does not use or link GLU, so libglu1-mesa-dev /
GLU is NOT required:
  - Linux:   apt-get install libosmesa6-dev   (pulls llvmpipe)
  - macOS:   brew install mesa                 (provides libOSMesa + GL/osmesa.h)
  - Windows: a Mesa build providing osmesa.{h,lib/dll}


Build
-----

    cmake -DFREEGLUT_OSMESA=ON -DFREEGLUT_GLES=OFF -B build-osmesa .
    cmake --build build-osmesa

This produces the library named `glut_osmesa` (so it coexists with a normal
freeglut build) plus a self-test, `osmesa_selftest`, which renders with no
display and checks read-back and GL_FEEDBACK capture:

    ./build-osmesa/bin/osmesa_selftest


Notes / limitations
-------------------

  - Single buffer only. GLUT_DOUBLE is accepted but downgraded to single-buffer
    (glutSwapBuffers is a no-op; the draw buffer is pinned to GL_FRONT).
  - The context is always a compatibility context; glutInitContextProfile with a
    core profile is ignored (a compatibility context is the whole point).
  - GLUT_ACCUM, GLUT_MULTISAMPLE and GLUT_SRGB are best-effort/ignored on swrast.
  - No input devices, cursor, game mode, menus or window resizing
    (glutReshapeWindow does not reallocate the off-screen buffer).
  - Read pixels back with OSMesaGetColorBuffer(); with the Gallium OSMesa driver
    the finished image is not guaranteed to be in your malloc'd pointer until a
    flush. OSMesa's default pixel origin is bottom-up (OSMESA_Y_UP=1).
  - The general progs/ demos (which use GLU and assume a window) are not built
    under FREEGLUT_OSMESA.
